  "name": "Rather Brilliant Weekend",
  "shortName": "RBW",
  "description": "RBW, short for Rather Brilliant Weekend and formerly Red, Blue & White, was the UK's first furry convention and, at its peak, the second largest in Europe. It grew out of the annual Christmas meal of LondonFurs, a group founded in 1998, when Rapido took charge of the group in 2006 and replaced the meal with a much larger boat party on the River Thames. In 2007 it became a two-day convention, in 2008 it moved to the Royal National Hotel in Bloomsbury, and in 2009 it moved to London's Docklands and took the name Rather Brilliant Weekend, keeping the traditional boat trip at the centre of a full programme. It was held annually in London until 2010, drawing furs from across the UK, Europe and the US, and in 2011 only the boat party was run.",
